1
00:00:01,921 --> 00:00:03,298
Hoo, hoo!

2
00:00:03,410 --> 00:00:04,337
Hi!

3
00:00:04,387 --> 00:00:06,415
It's me, Popcorn!

4
00:00:06,536 --> 00:00:11,767
Welcome to Popcorn Tales, the
cozy nest of bedtime stories.

5
00:00:12,079 --> 00:00:15,516
Hug your teddy, because
tonight's story is:

6
00:00:15,566 --> 00:00:18,310
Popcorn's Trip Through the Planets!

7
00:00:22,896 --> 00:00:28,401
Once upon a time, on a very starry
night, in the blue house on top of the

8
00:00:28,451 --> 00:00:29,651
hill.

9
00:00:29,913 --> 00:00:35,633
Lara was already in her pajamas, but
she just couldn't close her eyes.

10
00:00:36,285 --> 00:00:40,999
Through the window, she could see a
little dot of light shining brighter than

11
00:00:41,049 --> 00:00:42,282
all the others.

12
00:00:42,928 --> 00:00:47,938
Popcorn, which star is that, shining
so brightly right next to the moon?

13
00:00:47,988 --> 00:00:50,541
Lara asked, pointing at the sky.

14
00:00:51,165 --> 00:00:52,541
Hoo, hoo!

15
00:00:52,637 --> 00:00:55,459
That little light isn't a star at all.

16
00:00:55,599 --> 00:00:59,264
It's the planet Venus,
one of Earth's neighbors!

17
00:00:59,314 --> 00:01:01,533
Popcorn answered proudly.

18
00:01:02,179 --> 00:01:06,843
Lara sat up in bed, her eyes
sparkling with curiosity.

19
00:01:07,494 --> 00:01:10,183
I wish I could see the planets up close...

20
00:01:10,233 --> 00:01:12,133
Lara said with a sigh.

21
00:01:13,234 --> 00:01:16,676
Popcorn winked and had a very fun idea.

22
00:01:17,363 --> 00:01:20,563
They took a big cardboard
box left over from the move,

23
00:01:20,613 --> 00:01:23,791
and they drew little round
windows on both sides.

24
00:01:24,425 --> 00:01:28,631
And Boris the little ghost came
floating down from the attic to help,

25
00:01:28,703 --> 00:01:31,867
and he switched on his
glow inside the rocket.

26
00:01:35,429 --> 00:01:39,650
Attention, crew, buckle up
your cardboard seat belts,

27
00:01:39,700 --> 00:01:41,421
and let's count together:

28
00:01:41,471 --> 00:01:44,718
three, two, one, and off we go!

29
00:01:44,768 --> 00:01:48,349
Popcorn said, flapping her little wings.

30
00:01:52,475 --> 00:01:58,847
And the cardboard rocket flew up,
up, up into the sky of imagination.

31
00:01:59,486 --> 00:02:03,691
The first planet on the way was
Mercury, the closest one to the Sun,

32
00:02:03,750 --> 00:02:07,316
tiny and covered in
craters, just like our moon.

33
00:02:07,911 --> 00:02:09,288
Hoo, hoo!

34
00:02:09,404 --> 00:02:14,681
On Mercury, the days are super hot,
but the nights are freezing cold!

35
00:02:14,731 --> 00:02:17,909
Popcorn said, shivering her feathers.

36
00:02:18,572 --> 00:02:23,508
Soon after came Venus, all
wrapped up in yellowish clouds,

37
00:02:23,558 --> 00:02:25,680
like a very thick blanket.

38
00:02:26,272 --> 00:02:31,144
Venus is the hottest planet of all,
and there the Sun rises on the opposite

39
00:02:31,194 --> 00:02:32,636
side from ours!

40
00:02:32,686 --> 00:02:35,086
Popcorn explained with a smile.

41
00:02:35,707 --> 00:02:39,023
So there I'd wake up looking out
of the other side of my window!

42
00:02:39,073 --> 00:02:40,987
Lara said with a laugh.

43
00:02:43,648 --> 00:02:48,270
The rocket made a little turn, and
down below appeared a blue ball,

44
00:02:48,370 --> 00:02:51,409
decorated with fluffy white clouds.

45
00:02:51,967 --> 00:02:56,933
Look, Lara, that little blue
ball is our home, planet Earth!

46
00:02:56,983 --> 00:02:58,952
Popcorn said warmly.

47
00:02:59,606 --> 00:03:02,712
Why is the Earth so very blue, Popcorn?

48
00:03:02,762 --> 00:03:06,259
Lara asked, pressing her
nose against the window.

49
00:03:06,861 --> 00:03:12,157
Because most of it is covered in
water, with huge seas and oceans!

50
00:03:12,499 --> 00:03:17,603
And it's the only planet we know
of with animals, plants and people,

51
00:03:17,653 --> 00:03:19,872
Popcorn answered happily.

52
00:03:20,534 --> 00:03:25,136
Lara waved hello to the blue house on
the hill, even though it was far too

53
00:03:25,186 --> 00:03:26,572
tiny to see.

54
00:03:29,210 --> 00:03:33,916
After Earth, the rocket came
close to a rusty-colored planet,

55
00:03:34,085 --> 00:03:36,541
orange and very dusty.

56
00:03:37,112 --> 00:03:43,182
This is Mars, the red planet, and its
ground is covered in rusty iron dust,

57
00:03:43,232 --> 00:03:45,451
and that's why it has this color,

58
00:03:45,501 --> 00:03:48,624
Popcorn said, pointing with her wing.

59
00:03:49,217 --> 00:03:54,271
And on Mars there's the tallest volcano
we know of, much taller than any

60
00:03:54,321 --> 00:03:55,732
mountain on Earth!

61
00:03:55,782 --> 00:03:58,044
Popcorn went on excitedly.

62
00:03:58,717 --> 00:04:02,878
Wow, imagine sliding all the
way down a volcano that big!

63
00:04:02,928 --> 00:04:05,953
Lara said, giggling behind her hand.

64
00:04:08,596 --> 00:04:13,491
Suddenly, the rocket's window was
filled by an enormous planet covered in

65
00:04:13,541 --> 00:04:14,741
stripes.

66
00:04:15,245 --> 00:04:16,622
Hoo, hoo!

67
00:04:16,719 --> 00:04:20,426
We've reached Jupiter,
the biggest planet of all!

68
00:04:20,685 --> 00:04:23,879
More than a thousand
Earths could fit inside it!

69
00:04:23,929 --> 00:04:26,898
Popcorn said, her eyes wide.

70
00:04:27,573 --> 00:04:31,207
And what's that big red spot over
there, that looks like an eye?

71
00:04:31,257 --> 00:04:33,324
Lara asked curiously.

72
00:04:33,964 --> 00:04:39,117
It's a giant storm that has been spinning
and spinning for hundreds of years.

73
00:04:39,434 --> 00:04:41,604
It's bigger than our whole Earth!

74
00:04:41,654 --> 00:04:43,887
Popcorn explained softly.

75
00:04:50,885 --> 00:04:56,113
Far away, Lara imagined the sound
of a very soft rumble of thunder,

76
00:04:56,172 --> 00:04:58,461
and she snuggled down in her seat.

77
00:05:01,098 --> 00:05:05,609
The next planet was so beautiful
that Lara couldn't say a word.

78
00:05:06,239 --> 00:05:11,537
It had enormous rings all around it,
shining like a ballerina's skirt twirling

79
00:05:11,587 --> 00:05:12,787
in the dark.

80
00:05:13,258 --> 00:05:17,636
This is Saturn, and its rings
are made of bits of ice and rock,

81
00:05:17,686 --> 00:05:20,639
some tiny and some as big as a house,

82
00:05:20,689 --> 00:05:23,103
Popcorn said, amazed.

83
00:05:23,696 --> 00:05:25,958
And do you know the funniest thing?

84
00:05:26,142 --> 00:05:31,249
It's so light that, if there were a
giant bathtub, Saturn would float in the

85
00:05:31,299 --> 00:05:32,038
water!

86
00:05:32,088 --> 00:05:34,377
Popcorn said, laughing.

87
00:05:35,067 --> 00:05:38,723
A planet floating in the
bathtub, next to my rubber duck?

88
00:05:38,773 --> 00:05:40,784
Lara asked, giggling.

89
00:05:43,528 --> 00:05:47,993
Farther, much farther away,
there was a blue-green planet,

90
00:05:48,093 --> 00:05:50,646
spinning while lying on its side.

91
00:05:51,188 --> 00:05:57,161
This is Uranus, and it spins lying down,
like a ball rolling across the floor,

92
00:05:57,211 --> 00:05:59,750
Popcorn explained with a giggle.

93
00:06:00,382 --> 00:06:03,018
It must be just as sleepy as I am,

94
00:06:03,068 --> 00:06:05,940
Lara said with a long, long yawn.

95
00:06:06,852 --> 00:06:11,136
And at the very end of the trip shone
Neptune, the planet farthest from the

96
00:06:11,186 --> 00:06:14,669
Sun, as blue as the deep sea.

97
00:06:15,272 --> 00:06:19,675
On Neptune blow the strongest
winds in the whole Solar System,

98
00:06:19,725 --> 00:06:21,879
even stronger than a hurricane!

99
00:06:21,929 --> 00:06:25,343
Popcorn said, holding on to her feathers.

100
00:06:25,977 --> 00:06:30,081
Then it's time to go home, before
the wind blows our rocket away!

101
00:06:30,131 --> 00:06:33,392
Lara said, holding on tight to her seat.

102
00:06:37,977 --> 00:06:41,718
The cardboard rocket turned
around and flew back slowly,

103
00:06:41,768 --> 00:06:44,182
until it landed on the bedroom rug.

104
00:06:44,841 --> 00:06:50,838
Lara climbed into bed, and Boris glowed
softly, like a little night light.

105
00:06:51,451 --> 00:06:55,688
Shall we count the planets very
slowly, like counting sheep?

106
00:06:55,738 --> 00:06:57,861
Popcorn whispered gently.

107
00:06:58,578 --> 00:07:01,673
First comes Mercury, then
Venus, then our lovely Earth,

108
00:07:01,723 --> 00:07:03,342
and then little red Mars...

109
00:07:03,392 --> 00:07:06,500
Lara said, more and more quietly.

110
00:07:07,096 --> 00:07:12,437
Then comes giant Jupiter, Saturn
with its rings, sleepy Uranus,

111
00:07:12,487 --> 00:07:14,376
and faraway Neptune...

112
00:07:14,426 --> 00:07:18,201
Popcorn added, in a very gentle voice.

113
00:07:18,853 --> 00:07:24,961
But Lara was already asleep, dreaming
of shining rings and colorful planets.

114
00:07:25,571 --> 00:07:31,523
Hoo, hoo... curiosity is like a rocket,
and every question takes us on a brand

115
00:07:31,573 --> 00:07:32,772
new adventure,

116
00:07:32,822 --> 00:07:35,333
Popcorn whispered to the stars.

117
00:07:35,978 --> 00:07:41,420
And outside, under the starry
sky, the crickets sang softly.

118
00:07:48,726 --> 00:07:49,926
The End.

119
00:07:51,633 --> 00:07:52,345
Hoo...

120
00:07:52,395 --> 00:07:53,420
Psst!

121
00:07:53,470 --> 00:07:55,041
Are you still awake?

122
00:07:55,195 --> 00:07:57,249
Did you like tonight's story?

123
00:07:57,360 --> 00:08:01,737
Lara and Popcorn showed us that
curiosity is like a rocket:

124
00:08:01,787 --> 00:08:06,601
every question takes us on a brand
new adventure across the universe.

125
00:08:06,897 --> 00:08:11,203
Good night, sleep tight, and
have the sweetest dreams.

126
00:08:11,499 --> 00:08:16,397
Grown-ups: if you enjoyed it,
please subscribe to Popcorn Tales,

127
00:08:16,447 --> 00:08:18,853
for more stories at bedtime.

128
00:08:19,156 --> 00:08:20,356
Hoo...

